Package: zufuzz
Title: Coverage-Guided Fuzzing for R Packages
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("pedrobtz", email = "pedrobtz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Instruments R code so that a coverage-guided fuzzing engine can
    search for inputs reaching new branches, and supplies the tooling around a
    campaign: a byte-driven data provider and R object generator, a harness
    launcher, crash artifacts with structured metadata, replay in a fresh
    process, and fingerprint-gated test case minimization. The engine itself
    is external and optional, so instrumentation, generation, replay,
    minimization and coverage reporting all work with nothing else installed.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    codetools,
    digest,
    jsonlite,
    processx,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: AFL++ (optional, only for engine = "afl")
URL: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zufuzz
BugReports: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zufuzz/issues
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
